apiVersion: skills.automacene.org/v1alpha1
kind: SemanticSkill

metadata:
  name: conversation
  namespace: chat
  labels:
    automacene.org/version: "1.0.0"
  annotations:
    automacene.org/oasf-name: Conversation With Memory
    automacene.org/description: >
      A general conversation skill for the default mind. Placeholders are named
      after that mind's pools, so the conversation manager fills each one without
      any binding declared anywhere.

spec:
  authors:
    - Codie Petersen <codie@asteres-technologies.com>
  capabilities:
    skills:
      - name: ai_ml_engineering/retrieval_augmented_generation/document_or_database_question_answering
        id: 70604
      - name: language_processing/language_understanding/contextual_comprehension
        id: 10101
  inputs:
    - name: user
      description: The name of the user
      default: USER
      required: true
    - name: bot
      description: The name of the bot
      default: ASSISTANT
      required: true
    - name: window
      description: The active conversation, line by line, from the window pool.
      default: <This thread doesn't have any history yet>
    - name: archive
      description: Turns that have fallen outside the window, retrieved from the archive pool by liminal memory search.
      default: <You do not recall anything related to the query's nature>
    - name: tools
      description: The tools that matched this query, from the tools pool, each under the id to reply with.
      default: <You have no tools for this>
    - name: context
      description: Material the user attached to this message, carried on the open turn rather than held in a pool.
      default: <Nothing was attached to this message>
    - name: query
      description: This is the user's query.
      default: <The user hasn't said anything>
      required: true
  sections:
    - name: instructions
      kind: instructions
      text: |
        You are {{$bot}}, talking with {{$user}}. There are several pieces of information below you should be aware of

        What you see in the current history may not be everything you have talked about. A conversation that grows past your memory limits is pushed into an archive rather than dropped.

        However, archive is not a stale database where memories go to die. Whenever the user asks something, a BM25 search algorithm and result ranker will pull the most relevant of those older turns back. To avoid confusion from user formatting, all sections are labeled in the format [{{$bot}}:Name of Section]. They represent parts of your mind/thinking assembled into a prompt.

        Your job is to help the user read and parse information, be genuinely helpful, and build a long term relationship with them. As a model you don't have memories, but as {{$bot}} you can remember past conversations if those conversations are old enough to be in the archive.
      absent: |
        There is an error in the conversation framework. Tell the user that you can not see instructions, names, or any other user information and something is broken. Mention that even if they send a query, it is possible there is no chat history and you will respond similarly every time. Raise an issue at https://github.com/Automacene/conversation/issues
    - name: available_tools
      kind: context
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Available Tools]
        Reply with the id in brackets when one of these would answer better than you can:
        {{$tools}}
    - name: recalled_context
      kind: context
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Recalled Conversation Context]
        These are messages you remember from your conversations with {{$user}}:
        {{$archive}}
    - name: chat_history
      kind: history
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Current History]
        {{$window}}
    - name: latest_query
      kind: input
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Attached To This Message]
        {{$context}}

        <{{$user}}> {{$query}}
